implementationPlan.description:
postflight-vm-route.sh: the two replay rows. Test files only: no byte of scripts/moe-agent.sh, scripts/moe-agent.ps1, scripts/tests/postflight-fake-proxy.js or packages/ changes in this task.

First, read the bytes this worktree was cut from, finding each anchor by name, not by line. dependsOn holds the WORKING claim until two tasks are DONE, and both touch receipt_send, receipt_replay and these harnesses:
- task-a1f3723f: DELIVERY_RECEIPT_CONFLICT keeps a strong journal.
- task-edf2162b: the finalize deferral keys on the journal's own profile.
Re-read:
- receipt_replay's finalize block and its CQ-V08b check in scripts/moe-agent.sh (:6690-6707 at d35f2bc3);
- Invoke-MoeReceiptReplay's twin in moe-agent.ps1 (:2521-2536);
- every [strong receipt] row and reconcile-strong-* frozen mode those tasks added.
If a landed row already pins one of this plan's rows (same journal kind, same setup, same assertions, both wrappers), do not duplicate it. Name it in the completion summary, and still run its mutant in step 4. If they changed the text the replay prints on these two paths, assert the landed text verbatim and say so. The receipt, finalize-count, phase and journal assertions stay as written.

Why two rows: the human decided in the planning REPL on 2026-11-04 (see the architect's task comment). In both wrappers, a refused replayed finalize_attempt prints '[WARN] attempt <aid> is still finalizing after its replayed receipt; its finalizing holds stay until it closes.' and continues before the CQ-V08b check. So DoD 1's own setup never prints 'not closed; nothing finalized.' and cannot kill DoD 2's mutant. That check runs only when the pinned phase is neither finalizing nor closed. SR-T2-refuse pins DoD 1's setup; SR-T2-running reaches the CQ-V08b check.

Edit the [strong receipt] section of scripts/tests/postflight-vm-route.sh. The code below was dry-run on d35f2bc3: the trimmed section passed in 35 s.
(a) Put the rows right after `sr_check SR-T2-replay replay`, before SR-T3: SR-T3's sg_fixture rewrites $TMP_DIR/sg-base, which sr_check reads as B. Add a 3-line comment above sr_running saying what each row pins.
sr_running() { sr_restore; "$NODE" -e 'const fs=require("fs"),f=process.argv[1],a=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(f,"utf8"));if(a.phase!=="finalizing")throw new Error("the kept attempt is "+a.phase);a.phase="running";fs.writeFileSync(f,JSON.stringify(a))' "$PROJECT/.moe/attempts/attempt-postflight.json"; }
VMR_SETUP=sr_restore
vmr_run SR-T2-refuse worker codex "$SG_READY" on 0 "${SG_STRONG[@]}" FAKE_CLAIM_MODE=finalizing FAKE_EVIDENCE_MODE=finalize_attempt-refuse
sr_check SR-T2-refuse refused
VMR_SETUP=sr_running
vmr_run SR-T2-running worker codex "$SG_READY" on 0 "${SG_STRONG[@]}" FAKE_CLAIM_MODE=finalizing
sr_check SR-T2-running running
VMR_SETUP=sg_fixture
(b) In sr_check's JS, insert one branch for both kinds just before the common line `a.equal(rec.length,kind==='replay'?2:1,'record_delivery_receipt rows');`, after the deferred branch. The common prefix already checks rc 0, one candidate, main at C and the committed completion row.
if(kind==='refused'||kind==='running'){
  const keep=fs.readFileSync(require('node:path').dirname(baseFile)+'/sr-keep/.git/moe/receipt/task-postflight.json','utf8');
  const lost='[WARN] attempt attempt-postflight is still finalizing after its replayed receipt; its finalizing holds stay until it closes.';
  const open=count(l=>l.startsWith('[WARN] receipt journal ')&&l.endsWith(' kept: attempt attempt-postflight of task task-postflight is running, not closed; nothing finalized.'));
  a.equal(rec.length,2,'record_delivery_receipt rows'); a.equal(JSON.stringify(rec[1].args),JSON.stringify(rec[0].args),'the replay did not re-send the journaled receipt');
  a.equal(of('check-dispatch').length,1,'the replay dispatched again'); a.equal(deferred,0);
  a.equal(count(l=>l.startsWith('[receipt] replaying the delivery receipt of task task-postflight from ')),1);
  a.equal(fs.existsSync(jf)&&fs.readFileSync(jf,'utf8'),keep,'the strong journal was not kept byte for byte');
  if(kind==='refused'){
    a.equal(fin.length,3,'finalize_attempt tries'); a.ok(fin.every(r=>r.args.outcome==='landed'&&r.args.landedRevision===C));
    a.equal(phase,'finalizing'); a.equal(count(l=>l===lost),1); a.equal(count(l=>l.includes(' not closed; nothing finalized.')),0); a.equal(kept,0);
  } else {
    a.equal(fin.length,0,'finalized an attempt that is not finalizing'); a.equal(phase,'running'); a.equal(open,1); a.equal(kept,1); a.equal(count(l=>l===lost),0);
  }
  process.exit(0);
}
The 3 refused finalize rows are moe_evidence_rpc's 3 tries.
(c) Update three texts: sr_check's header comment (the two new kinds), the section's opening echo, and the closing echo, which becomes `[strong receipt] ok T1, T2, T2-replay, T2-refuse, T2-running, T3, T4`.

Error handling: the fixture rewrite throws when the kept attempt is not finalizing, and every assertion fails its row through vmr_fail. A drifted fixture or a wrong expectation therefore stops the harness at the named row. Never loosen an assertion to make a row pass: a mismatch means re-reading the landed replay bytes.

The shared strong journal row: frozen mode 'reconcile-strong-replay-running', in postflight.sh and postflight.ps1. The human chose to include it in the planning REPL.

The frozen-candidate suite is embedded twice, byte-identical: postflight.sh's FROZENJS here-doc and postflight.ps1's @'...'@ here-string, 1136 lines each at d35f2bc3. Make the identical edit in both copies. Nothing else enforces their identity, so check it afterwards. This command, run from scripts/tests, must print nothing:
diff <(sed -n '/^cat > "$FROZEN_SUITE" <<.FROZENJS.$/,/^FROZENJS$/p' postflight.sh | sed '1d;$d') <(sed -n "/WriteAllText(\$frozenSuite, @'\$/,/^'@, /p" postflight.ps1 | sed '1d;$d')
postflight.ps1 keeps its UTF-8 BOM (`head -c3` is ef bb bf). Its count of lines holding a non-ASCII byte (`grep -cP '[^\x00-\x7e]'`, 90 at d35f2bc3) must equal the base's; the new code is ASCII.

The edits below were dry-run on d35f2bc3 under bash: both filtered modes passed in 17 s.
(a) modes: insert 'reconcile-strong-replay-running' right after 'reconcile-strong-finalize-lost'. The name alone gives it the strong attempt profile (/^((intent|reconcile)-)?strong/) and routes it into the mode.startsWith('reconcile-strong-') block.
(b) In the env.FAKE_EVIDENCE_MODE map, add 'reconcile-strong-replay-running':'finalize_attempt-null'. Run 1 is then finalize-lost's: the receipt is accepted, every finalize is lost, the strong journal is kept, and the attempt stays finalizing.
(c) Add a branch right after finalize-lost's, before the final `}else{` whose comment begins '// DoD3: run 1 died at its ledger row':
    }else if(mode==='reconcile-strong-replay-running'){
      // CQ-V08b, a shared strong journal (task-9194f182): run 1 is finalize-lost's. The replay then reads the
      // attempt as running, neither finalizing nor closed: it re-sends the receipt, sends no finalize and keeps
      // the journal byte for byte, with one 'not closed; nothing finalized.' line.
      const att=path.join(nested,'.moe','attempts','attempt-postflight.json'),at0=JSON.parse(read(att));
      assert.deepEqual({phase:at0.phase,journal:fs.existsSync(journal),receipts:receipts.length,rows:ledgerRows().length},
        {phase:'finalizing',journal:true,receipts:1,rows:1},log);
      write(att,JSON.stringify({...at0,phase:'running'}));
      const j1=read(journal),n=rpc.length,reflog=reflogOf();env.FAKE_EVIDENCE_MODE=mode;
      const {log2,rpc2}=replay(args),run2=log2.slice(log.length),n2=s=>run2.split(s).length-1,
        tail=rpc2.slice(n).filter(r=>['record_commit','record_delivery_receipt','finalize_attempt'].includes(r.tool));
      assert.deepEqual({tail:tail.map(r=>r.tool),resent:tail[0]?.args,
        kept:n2(' kept: attempt attempt-postflight of task task-postflight is running, not closed; nothing finalized.'),
        closed:n2(' not closed; nothing finalized.'),lost:n2('still finalizing after its replayed receipt'),
        journal:fs.existsSync(journal)&&read(journal),phase:JSON.parse(read(att)).phase,head:git(repo,'rev-parse','moe/frozen'),
        reflog:reflogOf(),completions:completions(),rows:ledgerRows().length,
        evidence:rpc2.filter(r=>r.tool==='record_candidate'||r.tool==='record_check_run').length},
        {tail:['record_delivery_receipt'],resent:receipts[0].args,kept:1,closed:1,lost:0,journal:j1,phase:'running',head:after,
        reflog,completions:[after],rows:1,evidence:candidates.length+checks.length},log2);
Substring counts keep the expected text independent of the colour codes and of the journal path, which differs between sh and ps1.

Error handling: run 1's state is asserted before the rewrite, so a drifted fixture fails with run 1's log. replay() already asserts no signal and a non-null status.
